{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:58:06Z","content":"**No, it will NOT work right now.** \n\nIn fact, any user attempting to access `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443` will fail at two distinct layers: **DNS routing** and **Nginx proxy configuration**.\n\nHere is the exact technical evidence gathered directly from the network and the reverse proxy:\n\n---\n\n### 1. DNS Mismatch vs Firewall DNAT (<span style=\"color:red\">**Connection Timeout**</span>)\n\n* **Firewall DNAT IP**: `109.62.62.18:9443` $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443`\n* **Public DNS Resolution**:\n  ```bash\n  $ dig +short extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  109.62.64.27\n  ```\n* **The Problem**: When a user browses to `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`, their browser resolves the hostname to **`109.62.64.27`**, **NOT** `109.62.62.18`. \n* Because port 9443 is only DNATed on `109.62.62.18`, incoming requests to `109.62.64.27:9443` hit a dead end and time out (<span style=\"color:red\">`curl: (28) Connection timed out`</span>).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Protocol & Port Mismatch on Nginx (<span style=\"color:red\">**HTTP 502 Bad Gateway**</span>)\n\nEven if traffic reaches the reverse proxy (`172.30.198.33`), Nginx will immediately return **`502 Bad Gateway`**:\n\n* Look at the active configuration in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n  ```nginx\n  # reverse proxy vers Map\n  location / {\n      proxy_pass http://172.30.198.50;    # <--- Requests HTTP on port 80!\n      #proxy_ssl_verify off;\n      ...\n  }\n  ```\n* **The Reality on `172.30.198.50`**:\n  * Port 80 is <span style=\"color:red\">**closed (`Connection refused`)**</span>.\n  * Centreon Map (Apache Tomcat) is actually listening on **port 9443 with TLS (<span style=\"color:green\">HTTPS</span>)**.\n  * When Nginx tries to connect via plain HTTP to port 80, the TCP connection is refused, yielding <span style=\"color:red\">**HTTP/2 502 Bad Gateway**</span>.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Context Path Redirection (<span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**HTTP 404 Not Found**</span>)\n\n* On the Map backend (`172.30.198.50:9443`), root `/` returns a Tomcat **404 Not Found**.\n* Centreon Map is deployed under **`/centreon-map/`** (which responds properly with `HTTP 401 Unauthorized` awaiting credentials/token).\n* Like port 443 redirects `/` to `/centreon/`, port 9443 needs a root redirect to `/centreon-map/`.\n\n---\n\n### Required Fixes to Make It Work\n\n1. **DNS / Firewall Alignment**:\n   * Either add a DNAT rule on `109.62.64.27` for port 9443 $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443`,\n   * **OR** create a dedicated DNS record (e.g. `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.62.18`).\n2. **Nginx Proxy Correction on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`**:\n   Update the port 9443 server block in `02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` to target the HTTPS port and handle SSL verification:\n   ```nginx\n   # Redirect root to /centreon-map/\n   location = / {\n       return 301 /centreon-map/;\n   }\n\n   location / {\n       proxy_pass         https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n       proxy_ssl_verify   off;\n       include            nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n       ...\n   }\n   ```\n3. Test syntax (`sudo nginx -t`) and reload (`sudo systemctl reload nginx`).","thinking":"**Investigating Unauthorized Access Issues**\n\nThe target resource is indeed live and accessible on HTTPS port 9443, as confirmed by the successful HTTP 401 response from the observed endpoint. However, the 401 Unauthorized status indicates a likely authentication issue when connecting to the API. Further examination is required to pinpoint the exact authentication failure causes.\n\n\n**Diagnosing DNS and Proxy Issues**\n\nThe current DNS configuration directs traffic to an incorrect public IP address, resulting in connection timeouts because the firewall rule is only mapped for a different IP. Also, the reverse proxy configuration is misconfigured, sending HTTP traffic to the backend server instead of HTTPS on the correct port, triggering a 502 error. These two independent problems must be addressed for this application to work.\n\n\n"}
