{"step_index":132,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:33:59Z","content":"Now that the public DNS record is configured, here is the exact roadmap to get Centreon Map live and working:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Clarify the Exact DNS Hostname\n\nPlease confirm which DNS entry you created:\n* **Option A**: Did you update `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to point to `109.62.62.18`?\n* **Option B**: Did you create a new subdomain (e.g. `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.62.18`)?\n  > [!NOTE]\n  > If you used a new subdomain, we must add it to `server_name` in Nginx (and ensure the SSL certificate covers it). If you kept `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, no certificate change is needed.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Fix the Nginx Virtual Host on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`)\n\nOn the reverse proxy, the port 9443 block in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) currently points to `http://172.30.198.50` (port 80 plain HTTP), which triggers an immediate <span style=\"color:red\">**502 Bad Gateway**</span>.\n\nWe need to update it with:\n1. **Target Protocol & Port**: `https://172.30.198.50:9443` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`.\n2. **Port Preservation**: Uncomment `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;` and pass `$http_host` so Tomcat redirects don't drop the `:9443` port.\n3. **Context Redirection**: Redirect `/` to `/centreon-map/` so users don't land on Tomcat's default 404 page.\n\n#### Updated Server Block:\n```nginx\n# HTTPS redirect MAP\nserver {\n    listen              172.30.198.33:9443 ssl http2 reuseport;\n    server_name         extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr;\n\n    # SSL\n    ssl_certificate     /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem;\n    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/privkey.pem;\n\n    # security\n    include             nginxconfig.io/security.conf;\n\n    # logging\n    access_log          /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-access.log;\n    error_log           /var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-error.log warn;\n\n    # Explicit root redirection to Centreon Map web app\n    location = / {\n        return 301 /centreon-map/;\n    }\n\n    # Reverse proxy to Centreon Map (Tomcat HTTPS on 9443)\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass                 https://172.30.198.50:9443;\n        proxy_ssl_verify           off;\n        \n        include                    nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;\n        proxy_set_header Host      $http_host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl   on;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port  9443;\n        \n        proxy_redirect             http:// https://;\n        proxy_headers_hash_max_size    1024;\n        proxy_headers_hash_bucket_size 128;\n    }\n\n    # additional config\n    include nginxconfig.io/general.conf;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Validate and Reload\n\n1. Test configuration syntax:\n   ```bash\n   sudo nginx -t\n   ```\n2. Gracefully reload Nginx:\n   ```bash\n   sudo systemctl reload nginx\n   ```\n3. Verify end-to-end with curl locally and from the public IP.\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to apply this configuration update to `02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` now?","thinking":"**Determining DNS Configuration Next Steps**\n\nThe user has confirmed adding a public DNS entry, but the specific hostname mapped to the IP address is unknown. The required next step is identifying which hostname the user configured in their DNS settings to complete the task. This step is essential because it informs the next action for moving forward.\n\n\n**Investigating DNS & Nginx Configuration**\n\nThe IP `109.62.62.18` might indicate either an update to the existing hostname, or the creation of a new subdomain. DNS TTL might be caching the old IP `109.62.64.27` if the existing hostname is used. A new hostname requires an `server_name` update in the Nginx configuration.\n\nNginx configuration on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`) must be corrected within the specified configuration file. The current Nginx configuration needs inspection to match the new DNS entry, checking the `server_name` directive, and verifying the reverse proxy setup. This configuration is critical for the application's functionality.\n\n\n"}
