{"step_index":158,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T08:37:03Z","content":"Awesome! Now that the DNS entry is created for Option B, here are the **next two immediate steps**:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Confirm the Exact FQDN Created\nWhat exact hostname did you create in your public DNS?\n* `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`?\n* `map.outremer-telecom.fr`?\n* Or another name?\n\n*(We need the exact string so we can add it to `server_name` in Nginx).*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Apply the Nginx Proxy Fix on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`)\n\nWe will update the port 9443 block in [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) with:\n\n1. **`server_name`**: add your new subdomain alongside `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`.\n2. **`proxy_pass`**: point to `https://172.30.198.50:9443` (with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`) instead of `http://172.30.198.50` to fix the <span style=\"color:red\">**502 Bad Gateway**</span>.\n3. **Root redirect**: add `location = / { return 301 /centreon-map/; }` to eliminate the Tomcat <span style=\"color:#d4a017\">**404 Not Found**</span>.\n4. **Port preservation**: enable `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;` and `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;` so Tomcat doesn't strip the port on redirects.\n\n---\n\n### 3. SSL Certificate Consideration\n\nThe active Let's Encrypt certificate currently only covers `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n* For immediate testing, clients will be able to connect (browsers may show a hostname mismatch warning on the new subdomain until we expand the certificate).\n* We can then easily add the new subdomain to the Certbot certificate using DNS-01 via your automated playbook.\n\n**Please share the exact FQDN you created, and I will back up and update the Nginx configuration on `172.30.198.33` immediately.**","thinking":"**Investigating Timeout, Confirming Hostname**\n\nThe connection timeout suggests a network issue. Internal workstations might have firewalls blocking external access, or the firewall rules could be incomplete. However, the exact hostname is unknown. Clarifying the Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) is necessary.\n\n\n"}
